<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pantaleimon Shpylka</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pantaleimon Shpylka was a Greek Catholic priest in the Lemko region of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carpathian-mountains">Carpathians</a>. After the collapse of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austria-Hungary</a> in 1918 he led the council of the Komancza Republic, a short-lived Lemko self-government around Komańcza that looked to the West Ukrainian People's Republic. Polish forces ended the republic in January 1919.</p></div>
